Wichar pre and classical sewage systems.
The ancient Wichar civilizations would use their sewing as a very simple system, their roads were made as canals, they would have stepping stones larger for people to cross roads from one side to the other, the roads were made to transport the dirty water and human waste simply direct them to cesspits strategically put around the cities, or then were sent out the cities walls quite simply.
The roads of stone would act to transport the water and waste, it was reclined and a bit deep, the people would simple throw any waste and residues into the roads and it would be taken away and always in specific hours as the waters would flow to take it off and guide the waters, in case of larger urban centers to cesspits while more less developed cities and villages the waste was simply thrown away outside the cities. They would have their own depots of water to periodically sweep off the waste.
left sidewalk. stepping stone. right sidewalk.
