After a cycle of 6 months the Minka, Minga would clean up the roads and use the sludge as fertilizer. Despite this the canals of irrigation and sewing were seemed as very different, In fact the water which would not go for the irrigation, was to clean up waste or then they would use the rain, mostly.
it was a general model for all wichar and Altiplano civilizations and from the Chullako, Vikán to the Potao and Tuyuchi they all shared the identical systems.

